mina_cs: FYI GreenHarbor onboarding failing with short bursts of 429s right after enabling the browser extension + app load. They get a handful of 429s for ~5-8s then normal. Any quick wins?

sara_support: Do we have a sample response or headers from one of the 429s?

mina_cs: They pasted this: 
```
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json
x-rw-limit: 120;window=60
x-rw-burst: 40;window=1
Body: {"error":"rate_limited","reason":"preflight_concurrency"}
```
GreenHarbor says extension + web app both initialize the SDK at the same time on first-load.

ryan_eng: That combination will cause duplicated preflight handshakes (service worker + page + extension). Common pattern: multiple contexts all calling ephemeral token endpoint simultaneously.

leo_se: Quick mitigations: (1) coalesce ephemeral fetches in the extension to avoid duplicate token calls, (2) enable a short client-side backoff/jitter on init, (3) consider increasing ephemeral token TTL for first-use flow.

ryan_eng: Example small change for the web app (pseudo): 
```
// coalesce token fetches across tabs (shared via BroadcastChannel)
const channel = new BroadcastChannel('rw_token');
let tokenPromise = null;
function getEphemeralToken() {
  if (tokenPromise) return tokenPromise;
  tokenPromise = fetch('/api/ephemeral').then(r=>r.json());
  tokenPromise.then(t=> channel.postMessage(t)).catch(()=>{ tokenPromise=null });
  return tokenPromise;
}
channel.onmessage = (m)=>{ /* accept token from other tab */ };
```
This prevents three separate preflight handshakes when the extension and page race.

sara_support: They can also turn on `init.throttleMs: 100` in SDK until they verify the extension handshake logic.

mina_cs: GreenHarbor tried `init.throttleMs:150` in staging and the 429 bursts evaporated.

ratebot: rate-limiter alert: 5s spike window at 3123460120 - peak 42 reqs/s - source: browser-extension+page.combo

leo_se: We'll add a short note to the onboarding playbook: "When customers use extensions or service workers, advise token coalescing (BroadcastChannel/localStorage) or SDK init throttling to avoid preflight storms."

ryan_eng: Also opened a tiny SDK improvement ticket to expose an out-of-the-box TokenCoalescer util and default `init` throttle for browser builds. Ticket: RW-UI-4321.

mina_cs: GreenHarbor will push to prod tomorrow morning. I'll monitor and reopen if needed. Thanks team :pray:

sara_support: Adding a troubleshooting snippet to the quickstart: check `x-rw-burst`, confirm single token fetch per user session, and watch for extension/service-worker duplicates.

mina_cs: Closing for now — will follow up after prod rollout. :white_check_mark:
